# Per-machine dev overrides, read by the Rust shell in debug builds only.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored, so a fresh clone inherits nothing from it and keeps
# the `demo` default. Packaged builds ignore the file entirely.
#
# Rules: only CODENEST_* keys are read; a variable already exported in your shell
# wins over the file; there are no inline comments — everything after the first
# `=` is the value.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CODENEST_ENV — which database and app-data root `pnpm tauri:dev` opens.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   demo  (default)  data/codenest.demo.db — synthetic; `make seed-demo ARGS=--reset` wipes it
#   prod             data/codenest.db — inside the repo, so `git clean -xdf` takes it
#   work             ~/Library/Application Support/com.codenest.dev/codenest.db
#
# `work` is the one to use for real task tracking. It keeps its own database,
# workspace and org-agents outside the repo and outside the packaged app's
# directory, so neither a repo clean nor wiping com.codenest.dashboard/ (the
# clean-first-run test) can destroy it.
#CODENEST_ENV=work

# Absolute database path; overrides CODENEST_ENV's choice of file. The app-data
# root still follows CODENEST_ENV, so this splits the two apart — normally leave
# it unset.
#CODENEST_DB_PATH=/absolute/path/to/codenest.db
